BEFORE -- the live tree, three argv cases. ALL SEVEN ARE rc=3 FOR ALL THREE, so the module
scope is what makes `--help` and a bad flag indistinguishable from no argv.

file                             none  --help   bad
checks/dup-census.py                3       3     3
checks/dup-gate.py                  3       3     3
checks/gate.py                      3       3     3
checks/hermetic-census.py           3       3     3
checks/nl-gate-noguard.py           3       3     3
checks/nl-gate.py                   3       3     3
checks/rn-gate.py                   3       3     3

AFTER -- refusal hoisted into `__moved_refuse__()`, called AFTER `parse_args()`

file                             none  --help   bad   no-argv says                            
checks/dup-census.py                1       1     1   FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such fil
checks/dup-gate.py                  1       1     1   FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such fil
checks/gate.py                      1       0     2   Node.js v26.8.1
checks/hermetic-census.py           1       1     1   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'is
checks/nl-gate-noguard.py           0       0     2   
checks/nl-gate.py                   1       0     2   
checks/rn-gate.py                   1       1     1   FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such fil

MODULE-SCOPE WORK THE REFUSAL STANDS IN FRONT OF -- this decides the fix's SHAPE

file                           module-scope work beyond the guard
checks/dup-census.py           exec_module, sys.path.insert
checks/dup-gate.py             exec_module
checks/gate.py                 sys.path.insert
checks/hermetic-census.py      exec_module, sys.path.insert, import graphcmp/isolate
checks/nl-gate-noguard.py      exec_module
checks/nl-gate.py              exec_module
checks/rn-gate.py              exec_module
